 "conventions": "SG-W4' step 0: exact 5L -> (bubble x 4L W4-spoke eta-family) map.  Pure python, exact (fractions).\n\nFor each pilot master: reconstruct the 5L vacuum graph from the 15-slot family 44b030da, glue the chosen\nbubble pair (a, b) into ONE line of mass^2 z = 1 + eta (Kallen-Lehmann), contract a series chain line if\npresent, match the 4L core by explicit vertex isomorphism to W4 (P14/PR11 native RustFlow family, eta on\nslot 1 = spoke) or to W4 with one edge contracted (subsector), solve the exact loop-momentum map\nk_5L = A (K_0..K_3, l), and rewrite numerators (rank-1 bubble rule, l^2 pinch -> T1 x product).\n\nOutput (map.json), per master, a list of terms; value (raw = Minkowski, measure d^dk/(i pi^(d/2)) per loop,\nno exp(gamma eps)):\n  I_raw = sum_terms coeff * X_term, where for kind 'spectral':\n     X = (-1)^(na+nb+1) (1/2 pi i) int_Gamma dz W_E^{(na,nb)}(z) * (z-1)^(-chain_n) * poly_eta(z-1) * V_T(z)\n     V_T(z) = RustFlow raw value of 4L family integral T (eta line slot 1, mass^2 = 1 + eta = z)\n  kind 'chain_const': X = (-1)^(na+nb+1) (1/2 pi i) int_Gamma W_E(z) (z-1)^(-m) dz * V_T(eta=0)\n  kind 'product_T1': X = T1_raw * V_T (T has slot-1 power 0: eta independent).\n",
